# Cross-origin isolation, which this page cannot run without.
#
# scsynth is compiled with pthreads and needs SharedArrayBuffer, and a page
# only gets SharedArrayBuffer when it is CROSS-ORIGIN ISOLATED. These two
# headers are what grant that. Without them the page still loads, draws, and
# runs its menus -- the log simply stops at "loading scsynth.wasm and
# sclang.wasm ..." and no audio ever arrives. Measured, by serving this exact
# build with the two lines removed:
#
#     crossOriginIsolated   false
#     SharedArrayBuffer     undefined
#     audio                 never
#
# A page that looks completely fine and is deaf, which is why this file is
# worth more comment than it is long.
#
# FORMAT: Cloudflare Pages and Netlify both read a `_headers` file at the
# root of the published directory, with the same syntax, so this one file
# serves either. Vercel wants the same two headers in `vercel.json`, Firebase
# in `firebase.json`, and GitHub Pages cannot do it at all.
#
# It must reach the published root: `public/` is copied into the build
# wholesale by vite, so this lands at `dist/_headers`. The hosts read it and
# do not serve it.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
